 //Data Binding
 1. Interpolation -> {{}}
 2.One way data binding-> [model]="model" or bind-target="model" (from componet to template)
 3.Event Binding->  (click)="anyFunction()" or on-target="anyFunction()"
 4.Two way data binding- [(model)]="model"
 
 Angular 2 follows Unidirectional data binding (either component to template or template to component). Below are the benifits.
 1.No more $apply API call required
 2. No more $digest cycle
 3. No more $watch cycle to be executed
 4. Hence no performance issue with digest and wather cycle.
 
 ** {{model | json}} will display complete object details of that property. (ex- {"id":1, "name":"xyz"})
** <pre>{{model | json}}</pre>    will format the data in JSON format.
ex {
     "id":1,
     "name":"xyz"
   }
** when ever we want to define any html attribute or class or style dynamically, we have to write code like
<button [attr.visible]="isVisible">ok</button>
<input type="text" [class.red]="isDanger"/> // if isDanger property is true then red css class will be applied to the textbox.
<input type="text" [style.coror]="isDanger?'red':'green'"/>
 
 **EventEmitter raises a new event. and the emit function inside the EventEmitted function will process that event emitting an output.
 
 *changing label text on change of textbox value in one way binding
 <label for="txtName"/>
 <input type="text" id="txtName" [value]="model.name" (input)="$event.target.value"/>
 
 (input)="$event.target.value" piece of code represents - on change of textbox value label text will also change as they are linked via id.
 
 
